# The compiler matrix for Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-FP8 on one RTX 5090: one request, text only, a BF16 trunk, the FP8
# weights kept coded, and the MTP head drafting two tokens, so a verify step holds three rows. This file names the
# programs the golden must cover, so `emmy trace --serving-twins` and `emmy eval golden` read it; SERVE_NATIVE adds
# native generation's programs (`emmy serve --runner generate --native`, one request), traced with SERVE_EXPERTS_GPU
# of the 256 routed experts per layer on the card (the boot's EMMY_GEN_EXPERTS_GPU). The KV cache is FP8 e4m3, which
# native's rotary and attention programs store and read.
SERVE_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-FP8
SERVE_REVISION=95a723d08a9490559dae23d0cff1d9466213d989
SERVE_GPU="NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5090"
SERVE_GOLDEN_FILE=recipes/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-FP8/golden/rtx5090_sm120.json
SERVE_MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS=64
SERVE_DECODE_BUCKET=4
SERVE_PREFILL_BUCKET=64
# No width-1 decode tier: the decode bucket serves single-token steps too.
SERVE_M1_TIER=0
SERVE_EXTRA_ARGS="--dtype bfloat16 --kv-cache-dtype fp8 --speculative-config '{\"method\":\"mtp\",\"num_speculative_tokens\":2}'"
SERVE_NATIVE=1
SERVE_EXPERTS_GPU=128
